From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: arm64: dts: h713: hy320: crust as the ARISC firmware's name

The tree names hy320-crust.bin (crust's h713_hy320_sr_defconfig, board id
4) instead of the vendor's h713-arisc.bin, as 0246 did for the HY200
QZ713DF A1, so that build-all's crust gate (release/check-crust.py:
firmware-name[0] == <board>-crust.bin) accepts an image that carries it.
The images still run the vendor firmware by default (the module option
firmware=vendor) because of the power supply's hum under crust (TODO
2.42); h713-arisc set crust switches. Experimental: crust has not run on
this board, and its HDMI socket is receiver port 1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff -u a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy320.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy320.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy320.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy320.dts
@@ -29,8 +29,8 @@
  *  - The focus motor is disabled under stock: off here.
  *  - The accelerometer at 0x18 on twi1 is an STK8BA58 (stk,stk83xx, chip
  *    ID 0x87), not the HY310's SC7A20: stk8ba50 drives it.
- *  - The display firmware's elog addresses, the vendor ARISC image, and no
- *    display MIPS restart (measured on the HY310 only).
+ *  - The display firmware's elog addresses, and no display MIPS restart
+ *    (measured on the HY310 only).
  *
  * The same as the HY310 by its stock tree: power key PL4 (standby_param,
  * keyboard power-gpio), IR on PL9 (cir_param; its address list holds the
@@ -55,9 +55,15 @@
 	status = "disabled";
 };
 
-/* The vendor ARISC image, as on the HY300 Pro: crust has run on the HY310 only. */
+/*
+ * crust (h713_hy320_sr_defconfig, board id 4) when the image carries it,
+ * the vendor image otherwise (the module option firmware=vendor, the
+ * default of the images). Experimental: nothing of crust has run on this
+ * board yet, and its HDMI socket is receiver port 1, which crust serves
+ * generically but no board has exercised (TODO 2.42).
+ */
 &arisc {
-	firmware-name = "h713-arisc.bin", "hy310-edid.bin";
+	firmware-name = "hy320-crust.bin", "hy310-edid.bin";
 };
 
 /* The display MIPS restart is measured on the HY310 only. */
